// THE WILDERNESS FISHING SPOT (13 October). Suggestion #10 was "raw manta and sea turtle wildy near
// west drags", and until now both fish came from the Fishing Trawler and nowhere else - the skill
// guide said so out loud and the Fishing level-up messages at 79 and 81 told the player as much.
//
// WHERE. 0_46_56_41_48, which is (2977,3616) - the pond in the middle of the three Wilderness green
// dragons at (2973,3620), (2977,3611) and (2982,3618), three tiles from each. There is no real
// coastline anywhere near them: the nearest shoreline a player can fish from is 79 tiles away at
// (2912,3538), which is level 3 Wilderness and not "near west drags" by any reading. The pond's
// tiles carry a water overlay (flo 5) and are walkable rather than blocked, so the spot npc simply
// stands in it and the player fishes from alongside - which is how it looks in game anyway.
//
// LEVEL 13 WILDERNESS, from (3616 - 3520) / 8 + 1. Deep enough to be a real decision and shallow
// enough to walk out of, which is the point: this is a sidegrade to the Trawler, not a replacement.
// See skill_fishing/scripts/fishing_spots/wildyfish.rs2 for the rest of that argument.
//
// moverestrict=nomove and wanderrange=0, as every other spot in this build: a fishing spot that
// drifts is a fishing spot nobody can click twice.

[wildyfish]
name=Fishing spot
desc=I can see something big swimming in the water.
model1=compofishspot_8
vislevel=hide
readyanim=fishingspot_ready
walkanim=fishingspot_walk
minimap=no
op3=Harpoon
op5=hidden
wanderrange=0
moverestrict=nomove
category=wildyfish
